-- title:
--   The principal law of a sliced forecast path is the pushforward of contained progressions
-- statement:
--   Fix the data of OpenAI's actual fixed-spatial forecast setting: a natural number $m$; a finite type $G$; finite types $I_j$ ($j \in \mathrm{Fin}\,m$) and $n : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \mathbb N$; finite types $B_a$ for $a \in$ `LayerSamplerAxis I n` (the sigma type $\Sigma_j\, I_j \oplus \mathrm{Fin}(n_j)$); finite types $J_j$, real subspaces $U_j \le \mathbb R^{J_j}$ and bases $b_j$ (indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}(n_j)$) of the orthogonal complement of `euclideanSubspace (U j)`; reals $R_j, \sigma_j$, a `LayerSamplerScale` $S$ for $(B, U, b, R, \sigma)$ over $G$ (a structure bundling a positive natural number $S.\mathrm{value}$ with width and gap inequalities), and proofs $hR$, $h\sigma$ that $R_j > 0$ and $\sigma_j > 0$ for all $j$; a finite type $X$ with decidable equality; finite types $E_j$ (`Eout`); natural numbers $D_{\mathrm{mod}}$ and $L$; embeddings $\mathrm{spatial} : \mathrm{Fin}\,L \hookrightarrow G$, $\mathrm{kernel}_j : \mathrm{Fin}\,L \times \mathrm{Fin}(j+1) \hookrightarrow G$, and $\mathrm{block}_{j,a} : \mathrm{Fin}\,L \hookrightarrow B_{\langle j, a\rangle}$ for every axis $a$ of layer $j$ that is not short (`AllocatedDegreeActiveAxis short j`, where $\mathrm{short}$ is the predicate `allocatedShortAxis U b S.value`, true exactly of the axes $\langle j, \mathrm{inr}\ i\rangle$ with `basisAxisScale (b j) i` $\le S.\mathrm{value}^{j+1}$); a finite type $T$ and an equivalence $G \simeq X \oplus (X \oplus T)$; reals $W_{\mathrm{sp}}, L_{\mathrm{sp}}$; $N : X \to \mathbb N$ (`physicalN`); and reals $\tau, \delta_{\mathrm{slice}}, P, P_{\mathrm{bad}}, P_{\mathrm{pres}}$. Let `slice` be an `ActualFixedSpatialSlicedForecastPath` over these data (a structure bundling an `ActualFixedSpatialForecastPath` `slice.path` over the same data with a step $> 0$, kernel lengths and starts, and, for each index $k$ of `PrincipalTupleIndex B (layerSamplerDegree I n)`, a length `principalLength k` $> 0$, a step `principalStep k` and a start `principalStart k` such that the progression $\mathrm{start}_k + \mathrm{step}_k t$, $0 \le t < \mathrm{length}_k$, lies in $[0, H_k)$, where $H =$ `allocatedPrincipalSides B U b S`; together with further identities).
--
--   Then `slice.principalLaw` (the probability weights `principalAffineIntervalLaw` on `PrincipalIntegerTuples B (layerSamplerDegree I n) Empty H` built from these lengths, steps and starts) equals the pushforward (`fiberLaw`) of the product weights `principalTupleWeights B (layerSamplerDegree I n) slice.principalLength _` (the product over $k$ of `integerScalarCubeWeights Empty (principalLength k)`) under the map `containedProgressionTupleMap B (layerSamplerDegree I n) H slice.principalLength slice.principalStep slice.principalStart _ _`, which acts coordinatewise by `containedProgressionCubeMap`: a point $z_k$ of the cube of side $\mathrm{length}_k$ that lies in `IntegerScalarCube` is sent to $\mathrm{start}_k + \mathrm{step}_k z_k$ (on the single coordinate, as $\alpha = \mathrm{Empty}$), and any other point to $0$.
--
